[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: this script does not register or unregister UE during scenarios
[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: existing registered UE pool is reused for all scenarios
[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: no ping is used
[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: every active slot runs its own iperf3 client
[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: zombie UE are replaced in-flight, without repeating the scenario
[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: zombie detection uses uesimtun RX counters, not buffered iperf stdout
[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: each zombie/replacement is logged as diagnostic event
[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: target_host=192.168.1.211 base_port=5201 replacement_base_port=5251 tcp_bitrate_per_ue=1M
[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: iperf client start delay is 0.05 seconds
[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: connect timeout is 4 seconds; stall detection is 5 seconds without RX progress
[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: replacement minimum duration is 5 seconds; adaptive extension limit is 1 seconds per slot
[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: after planned slot end, late replacement is disabled and script waits for real iperf exit until process timeout
[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: post-duration iperf timeout rc=124 is accepted only when the client had RX and valid iperf output, and is logged as UE_SLOT_LATE_TIMEOUT_ACCEPTED
[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: iperf server-busy port rebind is enabled rebinds=1; server-busy does not blacklist UE
[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: global UE suspect list is soft; suspected UE are avoided first, but reused if the pool would otherwise be exhausted
[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: initial ramp-up starts all slots first; supervisor/replacement starts after initial slots are launched
[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: VPA hard reset is executed once before all scenarios
[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: after VPA restart there is no fixed sleep; script waits until UPF request_cpu equals idle value 25m before traffic
[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: UPF/VPA control monitor logs request changes, VPA recommendation changes, current usage and previous 5s sample every 1s
[2026-08-22T01:45:06+02:00] IMPORTANT: Metrics are still collected externally by Prometheus and Grafana
